WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.040
Carbon capture isn't real. Wait, yes it is! Here&nbsp;in Switzerland, a giant new machine is sucking

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:09.540
carbon directly from the air. Developers say the&nbsp;
plant will capture about 900 tons of CO2 annually,

00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:14.400
or the approximate level released from 200 cars.
Or how about the world's largest carbon capture&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:20.280
plant, Orca in Iceland, designed to filter up to&nbsp;
4 000 tons of CO2 a year? Yes these projects do&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:25.380
exist and they do suck CO2 out of the atmosphere,&nbsp;
but carbon capture as advertised still isn't real.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:31.020
Let me explain. So the Orca each year captures&nbsp;
4 000 tons of CO2, translating to about

00:00:31.020 --> 00:00:36.840
11 tons per day, or about half a ton per hour. Capturing&nbsp;
one ton of CO2 costs 2 650 kilowatt hours,

00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:41.460
or so they say. So here's the problem: the average&nbsp;
coal power plant spews out about a kilogram of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.460 --> 00:00:46.680
CO2 per kilowatt hour, meaning to produce those&nbsp;
2650 kilowatt hours necessary to capture one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.680 --> 00:00:51.960
ton of CO2, the average coal power plant has&nbsp;
to emit 2.65 tons of CO2. So if you run this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:56.340
carbon capture plant off a coal power plant,&nbsp;
you'll capture one ton, and produce 2.65 tons.

00:00:58.440 --> 00:01:03.240
If your fossil power plant is the cleanest type, i.e.&nbsp;
natural gas, and is brand new and efficient, you'll&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.240 --> 00:01:08.100
produce about 1.06 tons, practically breaking even.&nbsp;
Hang on a second, we have this thing called "green&nbsp;energy"!&nbsp;

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:13.980
If we run our carbon capture plant off that,&nbsp;
we no longer emit CO2! Problem solved, right?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.980 --> 00:01:18.540
No. If your energy mix contains any amount of fossil&nbsp;
fuels, your carbon capture plant will be consuming&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.540 --> 00:01:22.680
green energy that could have been used to replace&nbsp;
fossil fuel production. So if the carbon capture&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:26.940
plant eats one megawatt of green energy, now a&nbsp;
fossil fuel plant has to increase production by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.940 --> 00:01:30.960
one megawatt to cover the hole. And you obviously&nbsp;
can't increase green energy production at the turn&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:35.580
of a dial. You can't control the wind speed or the&nbsp;
sun's brightness. Okay but what about nuclear?

00:01:35.580 --> 00:01:39.660
It's zero emission, and we can increase production at&nbsp;
the turn of a dial! Sure, but we should already be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.660 --> 00:01:43.680
doing that. If you could turn up a nuclear power&nbsp;
plant to cover the needs of carbon capture plants,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:47.520
well then why are we bothering with the carbon&nbsp;
capture plant to begin with? Let's just turn up the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:52.320
nuclear plant by default to replace fossil fuel&nbsp;
production, thereby reducing CO2 emissions.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:57.060
Okay, then what about a power grid that isn't connected&nbsp;
to any other power grids, and that operates on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.060 --> 00:02:02.100
100% renewable energy. Like Iceland! Where the Orca&nbsp;
plant is, not coincidentally. If we plug a

00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:08.100
carbon capture plant into that grid, that's absolutely a&nbsp;
net decrease in CO2. Right? No. If Iceland 

00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:12.240
DOESN'T have enough green Surplus to operate Orca, you'll&nbsp;
have to build a solar farm, let's say, to supply&nbsp;it.&nbsp;

00:02:12.240 --> 00:02:16.800
But then why not build the solar farm in other&nbsp;
countries, to reduce their fossil fuel consumption,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:21.840
thus their CO2 emission? And if Iceland DOES have&nbsp;
enough green surplus to operate Orca, why not just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:26.280
move stuff like server parks or data centers&nbsp;
to Iceland from other countries, to run them off&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.280 --> 00:02:30.480
the green surplus, thereby reducing fossil fuel&nbsp;
consumption? And my god, we haven't even talked&nbsp;about&nbsp;

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:34.680
things like emissions from transportation!&nbsp;
At full capacity the Orca plant eliminates the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.680 --> 00:02:39.600
annual emissions of 870 cars. Do you know what&nbsp;
else can eliminate the annual emissions of 870&nbsp;cars?

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:44.160
A couple of new bus lanes and bike paths! And&nbsp;
you don't even need megawatts of electricity to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:49.080
operate those. So if you're a company interested&nbsp;
in reducing CO2, why not just help fund bus lanes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.080 --> 00:02:53.160
and bike paths instead? That's because these carbon&nbsp;
capture plants are part of the same techbro grift&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.160 --> 00:02:57.660
that has been going on for years now. I.e. you&nbsp;
don't have to change your lifestyle. You can take&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.660 --> 00:03:02.100
your three kids to three separate [sports] trainings with&nbsp;
your gigantic SUV five times per week instead of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:06.300
taking public transit. You can keep eating beef&nbsp;
and similar animal products every day instead&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:10.260
of switching to more environmentally friendly&nbsp;foods.  
Because by the power of the Science God&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.260 --> 00:03:15.000
there's this plant somewhere that sucks the CO2&nbsp;
you produce out of the air through the magic of&nbsp;science.&nbsp;

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:19.020
This would be the equivalent of you taking&nbsp;
a crap in the middle of your living room instead&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.020 --> 00:03:23.460
of walking all the way to the toilet, so some&nbsp;
company announces a brand new AI enhanced&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.460 --> 00:03:28.380
$hit-cleaner Roomba to keep your living room tidy.&nbsp;
No, just stop $hitting on the floor! Go to the toilet!&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.380 --> 00:03:32.700
And if you don't have one, build one! And this is why&nbsp;
carbon capture isn't real. And by this I mean the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.700 --> 00:03:37.140
concept of carbon capture being a good alternative&nbsp;
to other measures. The technology itself is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.140 --> 00:03:42.120
of course real. It's just pointless as things stand now.&nbsp;
